/-  BraggH100.lean -- FIRST kernel-certified truncated Bragg amplitude.

    The finite-volume diffraction amplitude of the certified zeta zeros at the
    rational frequency u* = 693147/1000000 (~= log 2):

        F_100(u*) := sum_{k=1}^{29} cos(gamma_k * u*)

    over the N = 29 nontrivial zeros gamma_k with 0 < gamma_k <= 100.  Proven to lie
    in the certified interval

        F_100(u*) in [-3539047433834710954643978786391/500000000000000000000000000000, -3539027332571167731826985093079/500000000000000000000000000000]
        (~= [-7.0780948677, -7.0780546651], width 4.02e-05;
         float truth -7.0780747664).

    STRUCTURE (all kernel-checked, no sorry):
      * Each zero gamma_k is re-derived by the IVT from a certified sign change of
        gLine = Re Lambda(1/2+it) across a rational bracket [a_k, b_k] (width ~1e-6) --
        the same mechanism as XiLineZeros; the endpoint signs (`henc*`) are the
        documented Arb non-kernel input (`enclose_lambda`), identical trust class to
        the band `hLine`.
      * cos(gamma_k*u*) is enclosed by the CosEnclosure double-angle chain (base order-4
        Taylor at |y|<=1, M=30 doublings) at the sample c_k, then the bracket width is
        absorbed by the Lipschitz bound |cos x - cos y| <= |x - y|.
      * The 29 cos boxes are interval-folded (CosEnclosure.add_encl).

    COMPLETENESS (honest scope).  The winding certificate `AllZeros_h100` establishes
    that there are EXACTLY 29 nontrivial zeros up to height 100 and all lie on the line;
    the 29 ordinates witnessed here are those zeros.  This theorem is stated over the 29
    CERTIFIED ordinates (the set `hLine` carries).  Promoting `sum over witnesses` to
    `sum over the abstract zero set` needs a pigeonhole/injectivity step tying the
    winding Finset to these witnesses -- NOT done here; see the relay note.

    conjecture1_proved = False.  Finite-T diffraction snapshot only.
-/
